WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.215 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
AstralDeep is an open ecosystem for agents
that can do useful work.

2
00:00:05.335 --> 00:00:09.957 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
We're building it around a simple goal:
people should understand what an agent can

3
00:00:09.957 --> 00:00:11.479 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
do, even when it delegates.

4
00:00:12.149 --> 00:00:17.095 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
An agent may discover a tool, ask another
agent for help, or act on sensitive

5
00:00:17.095 --> 00:00:17.866 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
information.

6
00:00:17.986 --> 00:00:21.079 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
Each step needs a clear identity and
permission boundary.

7
00:00:21.199 --> 00:00:24.613 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
Finding a capability should never grant
permission to use it.

8
00:00:25.283 --> 00:00:29.101 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
With LETS enforcement enabled, delegation
has explicit limits.

9
00:00:29.221 --> 00:00:34.186 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
A child lease receives only a bounded share
of its parent's authority and resource

10
00:00:34.186 --> 00:00:35.579 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
budget, with an expiry.

11
00:00:35.699 --> 00:00:40.349 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
The executor verifies and durably claims a
receipt before the protected action.

12
00:00:41.019 --> 00:00:46.539 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
AstralDeep's design keeps identity, tool
policy, and owner isolation on the normal

13
00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:47.481 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
dispatch path.

14
00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:51.313 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
Sensitive actions need the appropriate
checks and confirmation.

15
00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:55.568 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
Audit provenance helps explain who
authorized an action and how authority

16
00:00:55.568 --> 00:00:56.191 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
reached it.

17
00:00:56.861 --> 00:01:00.061 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
Useful agents also need useful interfaces.

18
00:01:00.181 --> 00:01:05.450 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
A model can propose a form, table, or chart
using structured UI primitives.

19
00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:10.789 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
Code checks component types and references,
bounds the layout, and escapes web content

20
00:01:10.789 --> 00:01:11.821 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
before rendering.

21
00:01:11.941 --> 00:01:14.202 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
The model proposes. Code decides.

22
00:01:14.872 --> 00:01:17.667 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
AstralPrimitives defines the vocabulary.

23
00:01:17.787 --> 00:01:21.883 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
AstralProjection renders and adapts it for
web and native clients.

24
00:01:22.003 --> 00:01:26.269 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
AstralDeep orchestrates the work, while
AstralPlane owns durable state.

25
00:01:26.389 --> 00:01:31.426 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
The goal is consistent meaning across
devices, with components other developers

26
00:01:31.426 --> 00:01:32.064 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
can reuse.

27
00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:38.296 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
We want these parts to connect through
standard MCP, Agent2Agent, and other agent

28
00:01:38.296 --> 00:01:39.945 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
communication protocols.

29
00:01:40.065 --> 00:01:44.560 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
That means versioned contracts,
compatibility tests, and examples that work

30
00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:46.358 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
outside the full Astral stack.

31
00:01:47.028 --> 00:01:48.676 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
There is concrete work to do.

32
00:01:48.796 --> 00:01:53.776 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
Help test delegation boundaries, improve
protocol compatibility, or make voice

33
00:01:53.776 --> 00:01:57.543 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
survive interruptions and reconnects,
especially on mobile.

34
00:01:57.663 --> 00:02:02.935 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
Better primitive rendering, client parity,
and independent examples can make the system

35
00:02:02.935 --> 00:02:04.511 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
useful to more developers.

36
00:02:05.181 --> 00:02:09.341 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
The bounty board turns these goals into
tasks across five repositories.

37
00:02:09.461 --> 00:02:13.984 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
Choose a task, request a claim, and wait for
your reservation before starting.

38
00:02:14.104 --> 00:02:17.880 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
Accepted, reviewed work earns recognition
points on the leaderboard.

39
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.965 line:78% position:50% size:94% align:center
Join us at astraldeep.github.io.
